        {
          "text": "Written to `submission/main.c`.\n\nKey points on the implementation:\n\n- `k_timer_start(&one_shot_timer, K_MSEC(1000), K_NO_WAIT)` — passing `K_NO_WAIT` (zero) as the period is what makes the timer one-shot; a non-zero period would cause it to re-arm.\n- The expiry function runs in ISR context, so it only calls `k_work_submit()`, which is ISR-safe. The actual `printk` happens in the system work queue thread via `work_handler`.\n- `k_work_init()` is called in `main()` before the timer starts, since `K_TIMER_DEFINE` is a static definition but `struct k_work` needs runtime initialization (the alternative would have been `K_WORK_DEFINE`).\n\nI did not compile this — there's no Zephyr tree or build config in the workspace, so the code is unverified against a toolchain.",
